4.6.2 Circuit: 
Before wiring the LCD screen to your Arduino board we suggest soldering a pin header strip 
to the 14 (or 16) pin count connector of the LCD screen, as you can see in the image above. 
To wire your LCD screen to your board, connect the following pins: 
● LCD RS pin to digital pin 12 
● LCD Enable pin to digital pin 11 
● LCD D4 pin to digital pin 5 
● LCD D5 pin to digital pin 4 
● LCD D6 pin to digital pin 3 
● LCD D7 pin to digital pin 2 
● LCD R/W pin to GND 
● LCD VSS pin to GND 
● LCD VCC pin to 5V 
● LCD LED+ to 5V through a 220 ohm resistor 
● LCD LED- to GND 
Additionally, wire a 10k pot to +5V and GND, with its wiper (output) to LCD screens VO pin 
(pin3). 
